MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 8 feels like a useful next addition because its larger display offers video calling and convenient control of compatible devices alongside my home entertainment and security equipment.",
    "The smart plug offers a specific new use—automating a lamp—that fits my Alexa-enabled setup without duplicating my streaming devices."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another HD Fire TV Stick adds little when I already have a 4K stick and a Fire TV television; sharing the same ecosystem does not make it a useful addition.",
    "The camera bundles fit my security interests, but I have no current need for several more cameras. Echo Auto also lacks a clear purpose for me because my recent needs have centered on the home."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My use of Alexa-compatible products seems to have been taken as interest in almost any Alexa device, even when it serves a different setting or repeats an existing function.",
    "My camera purchases seem to have been interpreted as a continuing need for more cameras, without distinguishing a useful addition from an oversized bundle."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: a new device needs to add a useful capability beyond the streaming and monitoring equipment I have.",
    "I am selective about additions right now: I would choose the larger smart display over the smaller display or a speaker, and a simple lamp automation over several extra cameras."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my connected-home interests but sometimes confuse compatible products with additions I currently need."
}
